cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "IUM paper walkthrough: Colab notebooks reproducing in-situ ultrasonic monitoring of vat photopolymerization"
message: "If you use this material, please cite the article below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Yiquan
    affiliation: "ZIP-AM Laboratory, University of Pittsburgh"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wangyiquan1010-coder/IUM_paper_walkthrough"
abstract: >-
  A four-notebook reproduction and walkthrough of Wang & Zhao (2026),
  Additive Manufacturing 105300. The notebooks go from raw ultrasonic A-scans
  recorded during printing to physics-informed features, a three-branch
  attention-fusion network, and its interpretation, evaluated leave-one-
  intensity-out. The implementation is a simplified re-implementation written
  for teaching; the article is the authoritative description of the method.
keywords:
  - vat photopolymerization
  - additive manufacturing
  - in-situ monitoring
  - ultrasound
  - machine learning
  - process monitoring
